+    <p><em>Last updated: November 11, 2026</em></p>
+
+    <h2>1. Summary</h2>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is built on the principles of <strong>privacy by design</strong> and <strong>data minimisation</strong>. You can read every article without an account, without cookies, and without being tracked. We only process personal data when it is needed for a feature you actively use, or when you have given us your consent.</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li>No analytics or advertising scripts run until you opt in, and they never run on sign-in or sign-up pages.</li>
+        <li>We honour Global Privacy Control (GPC) and Do Not Track signals as a refusal of analytics.</li>
+        <li>Fonts are hosted on our own servers. Reading the site does not contact Google Fonts.</li>
+        <li>An account needs only a username and a password. We never ask for your e-mail address or real name.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. What we process, why, and for how long</h2>
+
+    <h3>a) Server access data (strictly necessary)</h3>
+    <p>When you load a page, your browser sends technical data such as your IP address, the requested URL, the time, and your user-agent. We use this only to deliver the page and to keep the service secure (legitimate interest). Our hosting provider keeps it in short-lived logs.</p>
+
+    <h3>b) Reading list (only if you use it)</h3>
+    <p>When you save an article to your reading list, we create a session cookie that holds the list of saved article slugs. No cookie is set before you use this feature. The cookie contains no profile information.</p>
+
+    <h3>c) Account (only if you sign up)</h3>
+    <p>To create an account we collect a <strong>username</strong> and a <strong>password</strong>, and nothing else. Please pick a nickname rather than your real name or e-mail address. The credentials are sent over an encrypted connection to our authentication service, which runs on Google Cloud Functions (as our processor). They are used only to create your account and sign you in. We do not track the sign-in and sign-up pages, and we do not cache or log what you type into those forms. You can ask us to delete your account at any time.</p>
+
+    <h3>d) Privacy choice (strictly necessary)</h3>
+    <p>Your analytics choice is saved in your browser's local storage under the key <code>dtt-privacy-consent</code>. It records the choice and the date you made it, and it is never sent to us.</p>
+
+    <h3>e) Analytics (optional, only with your consent)</h3>
+    <p>If you select “Allow analytics”, we load a script from our analytics service (hosted on Google Cloud). When you click a link or button, the script sends the element type (for example “link”), its visible label, and a timestamp. As with any web request, the service also receives your IP address. We do not collect form contents, and we do not use this data for advertising or profiling. Account and privacy controls are excluded from tracking.</p>
+    <p>You can withdraw your consent at any time with <strong>“Manage Privacy Preferences”</strong> in the footer. When you do, the page reloads without the analytics script.</p>
+
+    <h3>f) Advertising</h3>
+    <p>No advertising network is currently loaded. We will not enable one without first updating this policy and asking for your consent.</p>
+
+    <h2>3. Browser protections we apply</h2>
+    <p>Our pages send a strict <code>Referrer-Policy</code>, so other sites only learn our domain and never the article you were reading. We also send a <code>Permissions-Policy</code> that turns off the camera, microphone, geolocation, and interest-based advertising APIs such as Topics. Pages that handle your credentials are marked as not cacheable.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Your rights</h2>
+    <p>Depending on where you live, you have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your personal data, and to object to its processing. You may also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority. To use any of these rights, contact us using the details in our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/")}legal/imprint`}>Imprint</a>.</p>
